# Swift 6 Concurrency & Actor Isolation Rules

- ViewModels and UI state containers must be isolated with `@MainActor` and marked with `@Observable`.
- All data models passing across asynchronous task boundaries must conform to `Sendable`.
- Handle cooperative task cancellation with `try Task.checkCancellation()`.
- Capture `[weak self]` in escaping asynchronous closures to prevent memory retain cycles.
